  "prefLabel": "Plc 1906.01 Ethical and Professional Standards for Certified Doulas",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1906.01 Ethical and Professional Standards for Certified Doulas. Certified doulas shall:\n\n(a) Treat all individuals with respect, recognizing their unique identities and life choices;\n\n(b) Respect the dignity, humanity, and personal autonomy of each individual they serve;\n\n(c) Protect client information and maintain the privacy of each client’s information, unless directed by the client or required by law to release the information;\n\n(d) Act with honesty, fairness, and transparency in all situations related to practicing as a doula; and\n\n(e) Support each client’s informed decision-making and choices, and not impose the doula’s own preferences.\n\nSource. #14429, eff 1-16-26, EXPIRES 1-16-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1900.html"
